    "forecast_combination_puzzle": false,
    "summary": "BMA does NOT beat the best single model (EGARCH(1,1)-N). BMA QLIKE=0.548005 vs best single QLIKE=0.542960. BMA weights outperform equal weights, suggesting BIC-based model selection adds value. The highest average BMA weight goes to EGARCH(1,1)-t (0.998), indicating the data strongly favor this specification. Consistent with Liu & Maheu (2009): BMA provides modest improvement in point forecasts. The real value of BMA may lie in density forecasting and model uncertainty quantification. Limitations: (1) BIC approximation to marginal likelihood is rough \u2014 full Bayesian would use bridge sampling or thermodynamic integration. (2) Squared returns as RV proxy is noisy. (3) Single asset (SPY), single OOS period. (4) EGARCH-t may have numerical instability inflating its BIC."
